Simulacrum Admin: the flag-gated, local-only admin and debugging panel for the simulacrum (merc-mud) instance (docs/game/simulacrum-admin.md, the plan .ai-plans/active/2026-11-07_simulacrum-admin-panel). EVERYTHING here is reached only through index.ts behind `__SIMULACRUM_ADMIN_LOCAL__`, which main.tsx imports dynamically inside `if (__SIMULACRUM_ADMIN_LOCAL__)`: a production build must contain none of it, and scripts/check-local-only.mjs (pnpm check:local-only, run after a real production build) fails if the bundle marker or the dev vhost name is found. Never import a file from this folder from code outside it, and never from a module that is not itself behind the constant.

It is a SECOND local-only feature with its own switch, separate from Copilot's `__COPILOT_LOCAL__` (edge case LOCAL-04): do not import from features/copilot and do not read its constant. The switch comes from the PROCESS environment only (SIMULACRUM_ADMIN_LOCAL), never from an .env file (LOCAL-01).

The owner's LAN address is never written in this folder, its tests or its docs (LOCAL-05, an IP is Personal data); it is added at run time through browser storage.

The command catalog is two sources joined: commandTable.generated.ts (written by scripts/generate-simulacrum-admin-commands.mjs, never by hand) and commandSyntax.ts (by hand, from each merc-mud handler). When the game's command table changes, re-run the generator and then fix the entries commandCatalog.test.ts names. The set of commands that ask for confirmation is the owner's decision (docs/game/simulacrum-admin.md, "Which commands ask first"); do not narrow it without asking.

Testing gotchas for this folder and components/simulacrumAdmin/: (1) every test that sends builds a REAL sender with the injectable `dispatch` and a real reply collector under jest fake timers; the game "answers" by dispatching `game:remote-server:raw` and advancing 600 ms (the quiet period), so a test that forgets the advance sees `unknown`, not `done`. (2) The shared pieces (outcomeText, OutcomeView, ConfirmDialog, FieldInput, useConfirmation, CommandCard) have their own direct tests AND are exercised through the tabs; keep both, because the tabs' behaviour (values kept per command, a reply shown only for its own command and target) is not the pieces' behaviour. (3) Character names in fixtures are the placeholder `Testchar`; never a real one (PRIVNAME-01).

Naming gotcha for tests: the completion gate's quality check reads any `log.add(...)` / `log.clear()` as console logging and rejects the test, so activityLog.test.ts names its store `store`, not `log`. The module is called activityLog, but it is a plain store of sent commands, not a logger; keep that in mind when naming variables in tests that use it.
